.TH LINKMATE 1 "2026-10-16" "linkmate 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linkmate \- extract URLs from text and open one in a browser
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linkmate
[\fB\-\-pane\fR | \fB\-\-clip\fR] [\fIFILE\fR]
.br
.B linkmate
\fB\-h\fR | \fB\-\-help\fR
.br
.B linkmate
\fB\-V\fR | \fB\-\-version\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B linkmate
reads text from one of several sources, extracts URLs using a
conservative URL\-character classifier, and presents them for
selection.  If standard output is a terminal, an interactive
selector is opened and a chosen URL is launched in the user's
browser.  If standard output is not a terminal, a numbered list is
printed to standard output and no browser is launched.
.SH INPUT SOURCES
Input is taken from the first available source in the following
order:
.IP "1." 4
.B \-\-pane
or
.B \-\-clip
if either is given.
.IP "2." 4
Standard input, if it is not a terminal.
.IP "3." 4
The first non\-option argument, interpreted as a file path.
.PP
If none applies,
.B linkmate
prints usage to standard error and exits with status 2.
.PP
Note that
.BI "cmd | linkmate FILE"
reads from standard input, not from
.IR FILE .
An explicit pipe takes precedence over a file argument.  This
matches the behavior of most Unix filters.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display usage information and exit.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-pane
Capture text from the current tmux pane and use it as input.
Requires being inside a tmux session.
.TP
.B \-\-clip
Read the system clipboard and use it as input.  Requires one of
.BR wl\-paste (1),
.BR xclip (1),
or
.BR xsel (1)
to be installed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B BROWSER
Program to launch for a selected URL.  If unset,
.B linkmate
tries
.BR xdg\-open ,
.BR open ,
.BR firefox ,
and
.B chromium
in order.
.TP
.B LINKMATE_BROWSER_LOG
Path to a file where the browser's standard error is redirected.
Defaults to
.IR /tmp/lm\-browser.log .
Override this if multiple users share a machine, or to send
browser diagnostics somewhere you'll actually look.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.  URLs were found and either displayed or launched, or
the user quit the interactive selector without selecting.
.TP
.B 1
A runtime error occurred: an input source could not be read, or a
file could not be opened.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: an unknown option was given, or no input source was
available.
.PP
Note: "no URLs found" is not an error and exits 0.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B tailscale status | linkmate
Extract URLs from the output of
.BR tailscale (1)
and present them for selection.
.TP
.B linkmate README.md
Extract URLs from a local file.
.TP
.B tmux capture\-pane \-p | linkmate
Manually capture the current pane and pipe the result.  Equivalent
to
.BR \-\-pane .
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR xdg\-open (1),
.BR tmux (1),
.BR xclip (1),
.BR wl\-paste (1)
